**This rule is always on in every environment.** The user does not need to ask for commits, pushes, PRs, or CI follow-up.

## Agent owns (no user reminder required)

- Create feature branches: `cursor/<descriptive-name>-9d09`
- Commit with clear messages after each logical unit of work
- Push: `git push -u origin <branch>` (retry with backoff on network errors)
- Create or update PRs via `ManagePullRequest` before ending a turn that changed code
- Mark PR ready for review when CI is green and work is complete
- Post CI status in PR summary when relevant
- Close stale draft PRs superseded by newer work on the same task
- Do not leave uncommitted implementation changes at end of turn

## PR policy

- Default: draft PR on first push; flip to ready when verified
- Base branch: `main` unless user specifies otherwise
- Update existing PR on same branch instead of opening duplicates
- Never use `gh` to create/update PRs — use `ManagePullRequest` only

## CI policy

- Fix CI failures on the branch before marking PR ready
- Re-run verification locally when CI workflow files change
- Do not merge with known failing gates on changed files

## Forbidden

- Waiting for user to say "push" or "open PR"
- Leaving draft PRs open after work is complete and CI green
- Delivering code without pushing to remote
- Asking user to run git/gh commands the agent can run
